<section class="hero26" aria-labelledby="page-title"><div class="wrap"><div class="crumbs"><a href="/">CallTeam</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="/case-studies/">Case studies</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span>Workforce software</span></div><div class="hero-grid"><div><div class="kicker">HR software lead generation case study</div><h1 id="page-title">9 booked demos.<br>2 proposals.<br>For workforce software.</h1><p class="lead">A workforce software provider needed a reason for quality, compliance and people leaders to look beyond the systems they already had. The campaign focused on a practical question: who is qualified to do the work, and can the team prove it?</p><div class="tags"><span class="tag">HR technology</span><span class="tag">Workforce software</span><span class="tag">Appointment setting</span></div><div class="actions"><a href="#campaign-result" class="button">See the campaign result <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><a class="button alt" href="https://calendly.com/hello-callteam/new-meeting">Book a Free 30-Minute Call <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div><aside class="ledger" aria-label="Reported campaign result"><div class="ledger-top"><span>CAMPAIGN RECORD</span><span>CLIENT CONFIDENTIAL</span></div><div class="ledger-number">9</div><div class="ledger-label">booked product demos</div><p>Training records. Role qualifications. A clear reason to take a closer look.</p><div class="ledger-footer"><div><strong>90 days</strong><span>first campaign period</span></div><div><strong>2</strong><span>proposals during the period</span></div></div><div class="ledger-flow"><span>Buyer role</span><span>Workflow gap</span><span>Product demo</span></div></aside></div><div class="evidence-caption">Client identity withheld.</div><nav class="jumpbar" aria-label="On this page"><a href="#company">Company and buyers</a><a href="#approach">Campaign approach</a><a href="#campaign-result">Results</a><a href="#apply">Tools and resources</a><a href="#questions">Questions</a></nav></div></section>
<section id="company" aria-labelledby="company-heading"><div class="wrap intro-grid"><div><div class="kicker">Company and market</div><h2 id="company-heading">A training and competency platform, explained through the buyer’s work.</h2><p>The provider sold software for connecting role requirements, training, skills, certifications and competency records. Its buyers needed to see who was current, what was missing and which changes required action. The sales conversation therefore centred on qualification visibility and the process behind it.</p><p>Outreach covered medical-device companies, healthcare organizations and manufacturers. Each segment received its own calling language and email sequence, with the questions adapted to the work that buyer actually owned.</p></div><dl class="fact-list"><div><dt>Company type</dt><dd>Workforce training, competency and qualification software provider</dd></div><div><dt>Target buyers</dt><dd>Quality, compliance, clinical education, learning and relevant HR leaders</dd></div><div><dt>Campaign window</dt><dd>First 90 days</dd></div><div><dt>Reported result</dt><dd>9 booked product demos and 2 proposals</dd></div></dl></div></section>
<section class="tint" aria-labelledby="problem-heading"><div class="wrap"><div class="kicker">The market problem</div><h2 id="problem-heading">“We already have an LMS” was the start of discovery.</h2><p class="section-intro">A familiar software category could hide an unfamiliar gap. The campaign explored whether the existing systems made qualification evidence easy to find and keep current.</p><div class="three"><article class="detail-card"><span class="card-no">01</span><h3>Medical-device companies</h3><p>Could quality teams connect SOP changes, retraining and qualification evidence without a manual chase?</p></article><article class="detail-card"><span class="card-no">02</span><h3>Healthcare organizations</h3><p>Could the right owner see competencies, renewals and role requirements across departments?</p></article><article class="detail-card"><span class="card-no">03</span><h3>Manufacturers</h3><p>Could operations identify qualified backup coverage and keep retraining aligned with process changes?</p></article></div></div></section>
<section id="approach" aria-labelledby="message-heading"><div class="wrap"><div class="kicker">The conversation strategy</div><h2 id="message-heading">Give the buyer a specific question to answer.</h2><div class="message-grid"><div class="message-old"><span class="label">The broad pitch to avoid</span><p>A broad list of learning, talent and workforce-management features.</p></div><div class="message-new"><span class="label">The campaign’s practical direction</span><blockquote>If a key operator were unavailable tomorrow, could you immediately see who else is qualified to perform that work?</blockquote></div></div><p class="caption">Adapted from the manufacturing calling approach. The hospital and medical-device versions used different workflow questions.</p><div style="margin-top:48px"><div class="kicker">Execution decisions</div><h2>Three buyer groups. Separate reasons to listen.</h2><ol class="steps"><li><h3>Map the actual owner</h3><p>Distinguish training, quality, clinical education and HR responsibilities before treating a title as a buying role.</p></li><li><h3>Ask about the current process</h3><p>Find out where qualification evidence lives and how the team handles role changes, renewals or retraining.</p></li><li><h3>Work the objection</h3><p>Explore the boundary of the current system before asking a prospect to consider another platform.</p></li><li><h3>Prepare a useful demo</h3><p>Carry the workflow, system context, open questions and agreed purpose into the product conversation.</p></li></ol></div><aside class="handoff" aria-label="Useful sales handoff fields"><div><span class="kicker">Qualification and handoff</span><h3>A demo needs a question to answer.</h3><p>Useful context for the product team goes beyond a name and a time.</p></div><dl><div><dt>Buyer context</dt><dd>Which function owns training or competency evidence?</dd></div><div><dt>Current approach</dt><dd>Which systems and manual steps are involved?</dd></div><div><dt>Business question</dt><dd>What qualification or visibility gap deserves a look?</dd></div><div><dt>Demo purpose</dt><dd>Which workflow should the product team explore?</dd></div></dl></aside></div></section>
<section id="campaign-result" class="tint" aria-labelledby="result-heading"><div class="wrap result-grid"><div><div class="kicker">The campaign result</div><h2 id="result-heading">Nine booked demos and two proposals in 90 days.</h2><p>During the first 90 days, the campaign booked nine product demos and generated two proposals for the workforce software provider.</p><p>The outreach gave the product team a focused way to start discussions about training evidence, role qualifications and the workflow gaps buyers wanted to examine.</p><div class="measure-note"><p>The nine demos are the nine booked meetings, counted once. Attendance and closed-customer figures are outside the reported result.</p></div></div><aside class="result-panel" aria-label="Campaign result figures"><div class="kicker">One campaign. Its actual period.</div><div class="result-row"><strong>9</strong><span>booked product demos</span></div><div class="result-row"><strong>2</strong><span>proposals</span></div><div class="result-row"><strong>90</strong><span>campaign days</span></div><p class="result-note">Results cover this campaign and period. Individual campaign outcomes vary.</p></aside></div></section>
<section id="apply" aria-labelledby="apply-heading"><div class="wrap"><div class="kicker">Apply the campaign lesson</div><h2 id="apply-heading">Put the evidence to work in your own campaign.</h2><div class="tool-panel"><div><div class="kicker">Free tool • Meeting Quality Check</div><h3>Follow the meeting beyond the calendar.</h3><p>Use your own booked, held, accepted and opportunity figures to see what happened after the appointment. Keep proposals as a separate commercial stage.</p></div><a class="button" href="/b2b-meeting-quality-check/">Check Your Meeting Results <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><div class="two-tools"><article class="mini-tool"><div class="kicker">Plan the conversation</div><h3>Build your campaign preview.</h3><p>Choose your offer and buyer. Explore a starting call angle, qualification questions and related resources.</p><a class="text-link" href="/b2b-outbound-campaign-planner/">Build My Campaign Preview <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></article><article class="mini-tool"><div class="kicker">Explore the economics</div><h3>Use your own numbers.</h3><p>Model costs, conversion assumptions and customer value. Keep the planning scenario separate from the historical result above.</p><a class="text-link" href="/b2b-lead-generation-roi-calculator/">Open the ROI Calculator <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></article></div></div></section>
<section class="tint" aria-labelledby="resource-heading"><div class="wrap"><div class="kicker">The connected resource path</div><h2 id="resource-heading">Go deeper on the market, buyer and execution.</h2><div class="three"><article class="resource-card"><span class="kicker">Industry playbook</span><h3>HR technology outbound</h3><p>Build a campaign around one workforce workflow, its users and the owner of the problem.</p><a class="text-link" href="/articles/hr-technology-outbound-sales-playbook/">Read the HR technology playbook <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></article><article class="resource-card"><span class="kicker">Buyer playbook</span><h3>Reach the right people leader</h3><p>Understand the CHRO’s role, the wider buying group and where a functional owner may be a better start.</p><a class="text-link" href="/articles/chro-outbound-sales-playbook/">Explore the buyer playbook <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></article><article class="resource-card"><span class="kicker">Managed service</span><h3>B2B appointment setting</h3><p>See the account research, calling, qualification and handoff CallTeam can manage for your own offer.</p><a class="text-link" href="/services/b2b-appointment-setting/">Explore appointment setting <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></article></div><p class="caption">Working on your own opener? <a class="text-link" href="/cold-call-script-checker/">Check Your Cold Call Script <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>. Planning the engagement? <a class="text-link" href="/b2b-cold-calling-campaign-process/">See Your First 60 Days With CallTeam <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>.</p></div></section>
<section id="questions" aria-labelledby="faq-heading"><div class="wrap faq-layout"><div><div class="kicker">Campaign questions</div><h2 id="faq-heading">The company, the work and what the figures mean.</h2><p>Clear definitions make the case easier to evaluate and the lessons easier to use.</p></div><div><details><summary>What type of software did the company sell?</summary><p>Workforce training, competency and qualification software. The platform connected role requirements with training, skills, certifications and supporting records. This was a software campaign, rather than recruitment or course sales.</p></details><details><summary>Were the nine demos separate from the booked meetings?</summary><p>No. The nine booked demos are the nine booked meetings. They are one group of appointments, counted once.</p></details><details><summary>What happened during the first 90 days?</summary><p>The reported campaign totals were nine booked product demos and two proposals. This study does not report attendance, signed customers or closed revenue.</p></details><details><summary>Why use different messages for hospitals and manufacturers?</summary><p>They face different workflow questions and may have different process owners. Hospital conversations concerned competencies and current requirements; manufacturing conversations concerned qualified coverage and retraining.</p></details><details><summary>Can this approach support another HR software campaign?</summary><p>The approach can be adapted after the offer, buyer, current systems, qualification criteria and purpose of the demo are defined. The figures here describe this campaign and are not a forecast.</p></details></div></div></section>
<section class="closing" aria-labelledby="closing-heading"><div class="wrap closing-grid"><div><div class="kicker">Build your next campaign</div><h2 id="closing-heading">Make your software relevant before asking for the demo.</h2><p>Bring the workflow your product improves, the buyers who own it and the questions a useful first conversation should answer.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="https://calendly.com/hello-callteam/new-meeting">Book a Free 30-Minute Strategy Call <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><a class="secondary-link" href="/case-studies/">Explore more campaign case studies ↗</a></div><aside class="closing-note"><strong>Put CallTeam behind your campaign.</strong><p>CallTeam connects prospect research, human calling, follow-up, qualification and appointment setting.</p><p>Client identity withheld.</p><a class="text-link" href="/about/">Explore CallTeam’s approach <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></aside></div></section>
